    "content" : "Remark The restriction to β ≤ 1 in Theorem 3 was made just for simplicity. If the source term has higher spatial regularity, and if further conditions of the type (15) are fulﬁlled, then we can also show higher temporal order of convergence. The additional conditions can be derived by expanding the defect in (16) even further, and it can be shown as in Lemma 3 that they are implied by the underlying quadrature rule being of higher order. In particular, full (classical) order is achieved for suﬃciently smooth source term with periodic boundary conditions."
